{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade","id":1356964,"title":"What is a Shade?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-25T18:26:31-08:00","id":1356964,"title":"What is a Shade?","content":"So....cosmologically speaking, what do you think causes a soul to become a shade vs a ghost? Is a shade a incarnate piece of the soul (an, ren, ba. ka, etc?) that separates from the rest? Is it a being whose life and death were fundamentally different from what would create a ghost? An entity rich in Sekhem or cursed by fate? What \u201ccauses\u201d someone to die in a way that binds them to Duat when there isn\u2019t some asshole god thing performing a Rite to send them there? Canon and theories welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T20:25:16-08:00","id":1356976,"title":"","content":"<b>Explicit canon:</b><br /> Souls don't become ghosts. Ghosts are left behind by things that die (sometimes even when they die incompletely or for only a moment \u2013 Geist 2e introduces the ghosts of lost body parts and ghosts left by near-death experiences while the original person still lives). Dying is when the soul moves on from the body, but the ghost is not the soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Extrapolation/theory:</b><br /> Dreams of Avarice and Mummy 2e seem together to strongly suggest, but not explicitly assert, that all souls progress to Duat and that the pilgrimage of shades accomplishes this in some way. Souls found worthy by the Judges are meant to progress to starry A'aru, the home of the Scroll of Ages where all truths have already been recorded, and a place the Heretic describes as barren and empty..<br /> <br /> Mage has batted around the idea that souls are meant to join with supernal truth and then to reincarnate, but that in the Fallen World, this nature is somehow damaged.<br /> <br /> The ghost, by contrast, can be thought of as the memory or impression left on the world in a thing's absence, like the shape a heavy object imprints on a soft surface remaining after it is removed. This is metaphysically a bit more complicated when that impression itself has thoughts, feelings, and personhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T05:20:14-08:00","id":1357025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1356976#post1356976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Explicit canon:</b><br /> Souls don't become ghosts. Ghosts are left behind by things that die (sometimes even when they die incompletely or for only a moment \u2013 Geist 2e introduces the ghosts of lost body parts and ghosts left by near-death experiences while the original person still lives). Dying is when the soul moves on from the body, but the ghost is not the soul.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah. I remember hearing that somewhere. Still underwhelmed by the concept. &quot;Hi all you soul eaters out there! Are you tired of feasting on the delicious ectoplasmic filling of the recently departed only to gain ephermeral girth? Are manifesting in the physical realm and maintaining a regular exorcise program conflicting with your inscrutable agendas! The underworld has the solution for you! Introducing GHOST(tm), a new delicious artificial soul substitute with the same great taste with none of the empty ectocalories!&quot;<br /> <br /> My own misgivings and refusal to use ghosts as I-Can't-Believe-they-aren't-Souls in my own games aside....do you believe Shades are something similar? Another form of spirit &quot;echo&quot;? Or something completely different? Do we consider ghosts and shades as two subtypes of the same phenomena or wholly independent manifestations that happen to have memories of a mortal life in common? If a ghost manifests after someone dies, could that same death manifest a shade with the same memories as the ghost, for example, or does the manifestation of one preclude manifestation of the other?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T05:46:22-08:00","id":1357030,"title":"","content":"It seems like you're ascribing common properties to souls and ghosts that really aren't shared. &quot;I-Can't-Believe-They- Aren't-Souls&quot; implies a similarity that simply doesn't exist. The divide makes much more sense if you don't work from the assumption that they're the same thing (which they rarely are in RL religions, mythologies and folk lores).<br /> For starters, the soul does not house the seat of consciousness, while most ghosts are basically defined by the personality of the original person.<br /> <br /> Shades and ghosts occupy the same &quot;frequency&quot; of Twilight, but Twilight &quot;frequencies&quot; are actually different types of ephemera, each type only able to interact with itself. Since ghosts and shades inhabit the same &quot;frequency&quot; and can interact, they're made from the same type of ephemera (unlike that of spirits/idigam, or angels of the G-M). That implies ghosts and shades are tightly related and certainly not incidental to each other. How they're related, I don't know.<br /> On the same topic, it also means that dead (or otherwise disembodied) Arisen also are made from the same type of ephemera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T06:25:15-08:00","id":1357038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1357025#post1357025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeeeah. I remember hearing that somewhere. Still underwhelmed by the concept. &quot;Hi all you soul eaters out there! Are you tired of feasting on the delicious ectoplasmic filling of the recently departed only to gain ephermeral girth? Are manifesting in the physical realm and maintaining a regular exorcise program conflicting with your inscrutable agendas! The underworld has the solution for you! Introducing GHOST(tm), a new delicious artificial soul substitute with the same great taste with none of the empty ectocalories!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what you have a problem with here is not really the nature of ghosts in Chronicles of Darkness, but the nature of souls, since long before Mummy's shades were introduced. CofD games consistently characterize the soul as not being identical with a person (or, well, the parts of a person that aren't the body). You can remove the soul from a person and put a different person's soul in them. This <i>will</i> change them, but it won't be like replacing them with an entirely different person in their body. Their memories are the same, their long-term emotional attachments. The soul is more like a living energy which is necessary for a healthy person, which lives within the person and experiences their life and influences their nature and choices, but which is not simply an ephemeral brain or nervous system but something broader and less specific.<br /> <br /> The ghost is honestly more like what you're shooting for with the typical St. Peter at the Pearly Gates pop culture depiction of the soul as the person-without-the-body.<br /> <br /> The metaphysics of what make up a person, and the consequences of creatures being able to sever and reassemble those parts, are mysterious and unsettling in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1357025#post1357025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own misgivings and refusal to use ghosts as I-Can't-Believe-they-aren't-Souls in my own games aside....do you believe Shades are something similar? Another form of spirit &quot;echo&quot;? Or something completely different? Do we consider ghosts and shades as two subtypes of the same phenomena or wholly independent manifestations that happen to have memories of a mortal life in common? If a ghost manifests after someone dies, could that same death manifest a shade with the same memories as the ghost, for example, or does the manifestation of one preclude manifestation of the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do *<b>I*</b> think? Working off of what information we currently have, at least, I think the shade is a vehicle for the soul, the attachments and remembrance of living within your life become a thinking vessel to carry it to Duat. I don't think either the ghost or the shade encompasses everything that made a living person who she was; they are parts of the whole, and who you were in life was the result of a complicated interplay between many factors, the nature of your soul and the memories and feelings that form into your ghost being some (but not all!) of them. I think that likely every human who has not somehow lost their soul probably exudes a shade when they die (though perhaps not at the time and place where they die?), while many but not all humans who die (including those who are soulless?) leave ghosts.<br /> <br /> The soul and the ghost are parts of you, the living person, drifting apart into space after you die. Neither of them are you, the living person; you ceased to exist when you died. Both of them carry the mark of who you were and how you lived, in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T07:10:24-08:00","id":1357044,"title":"","content":"You're right about the soul in CofD. I don't think it corresponds to any IRL beliefs since anything that isn't intrinsically linked to a person (which the CofD soul isn't considering its plug'n'play nature), being that person's essence in some way, would ever be translated to &quot;soul&quot;. Calling it a soul is a bit of a misnomer.<br /> <br /> <i>On top of that</i> the ghosts in CofD comes from the modern paranatural belief that ghosts are basically psychic imprints or echoes of intense or dramatic emotions and moments, rather than any direct continuation of the person living on beyond their death; hence why less cognizant ghosts are stuck in loops and such behavious. Such ghosts have never been connected to souls IRL so it'd be weird if they were in CofD if CofD souls even did correspond to any RL beliefs.<br /> Reading CofD books with the pressumption that they should be connected or be the same thing is doing yourself a huge disservice since that isn't how it works in the &quot;source material&quot;, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T07:32:12-08:00","id":1357046,"title":"","content":"There isn\u2019t a canon answer for what a shade is at the moment. When writing them, I chose to leave it open for interpretation by individual groups. If I ever get the opportunity to tackle them in more depth, I might give a more concrete answer. I\u2019ve actually considered several different answers to the question, and I\u2019ve had a hard time picking a favorite. I think the simplest answer I\u2019ve considered would be to make them the Sheut of the deceased. I would probably favor a more complex answer if I was to write it up, but it fits well enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T07:45:43-08:00","id":1357047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1357046#post1357046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn\u2019t a canon answer for what a shade is at the moment. When writing them, I chose to leave it open for interpretation by individual groups. If I ever get the opportunity to tackle them in more depth, I might give a more concrete answer. I\u2019ve actually considered several different answers to the question, and I\u2019ve had a hard time picking a favorite. I think the simplest answer I\u2019ve considered would be to make them the Sheut of the deceased. I would probably favor a more complex answer if I was to write it up, but it fits well enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be very interesting to hear more about some of those ideas. Also, your thoughts on any potential relationship between vampires (specifically the Hollow Mekhet and their Ba) and shades, whatwith the whole gaining sustenance from blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T04:32:45-08:00","id":1357505,"title":"","content":"Shades do go to Duat to be judged, so they might be &quot;the part of soul that must be weighed for the Devourer.&quot;* Certainly they are more closely aligned with the occult forces of Sekhem than the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Mind you the Underworld is rather closely aligned with Memory, so that is a thing.<br /> <br /> *This is what I think the Iremite in-universe explanation is, not the canonical truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T07:33:18-08:00","id":1358857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1357047#post1357047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be very interesting to hear more about some of those ideas. Also, your thoughts on any potential relationship between vampires (specifically the Hollow Mekhet and their Ba) and shades, whatwith the whole gaining sustenance from blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not going to go into too much depth, since I don\u2019t yet know whether I\u2019ll ever get the chance to expand on them officially. I might even do something for the Vault for them eventually, if I have the time and nothing seems to be forthcoming about them in an official capacity.<br /> That said, many of the ideas still involve the Sheut, but with more complexity. For example, the Sheut bearing the Ab Pillar into Duat for judgment.<br /> As far as the vampires go, I gave exactly zero thought to them when writing the shades. The use of blood was a nod to the Odyssey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T18:37:14-07:00","id":1412659,"title":"","content":"This article had some interesting thoughts on Bronze Age cultures and their ghosts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.worldhistory.org/img/c/p/1200x627/3218.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ghosts in the Ancient World </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A belief in an afterlife was central to every major civilization of the ancient world and this encouraged the recognition of the reality of ghosts as the spirits of the departed who, for one reason... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rereading Dreams of Avarice I noted this passage: &quot;If you walk against the flow of<br /> Nebtet\u2019s blood it will dissolve you, and we five will fly to separate destinies. Your Shadow will howl in Neter-Khertet and the living will curse you. Your Spirit will invade your body and raise it to hunt the living who will burn you as an abomination. Your Essence will flow between Keb and Duat, to mingle in oases and holy places, and witches and unnatural things will devour it. Your Name will be forgotten and your Heart will sink alone to Duat, with no advocate, where She of the Countless Teeth will consume it.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if we assume the book accurately describes the fate that befalls non-Iremite educated souls, the Shadow seems like the best candidate for these Shades. The Ba survives, but seemingly animates the living corpse or otherwise lingers on in the physical remains. The Ka, perhaps playing of the similarity in names, seems to dissolve into magical energy that gets consumed by sorcerers, ghosts and spirits. No word about the fate of the Ren (odd) and the Ab falls into Duat and faces the Devourer. By this text a Shade could be the remnant of the Sheut, the Ren, or the Ab (since Shades are supposedly drawn slowly into Duat). Again, the shadowy nature seems to fit the Sheut best. That does beg the question if there are other ghostly entities out there born from the other pieces of the mortal. Also, I wonder about the general &quot;population&quot; of Shades- they presumably are fairly rare since Mummies alone know of them (likely because Shades are drawn to Sekhem). <br /> <br /> I also wonder if Shades ever serve cults the way the Blessed ghosts do/did in 1st edition. Do any serve the Devourer? How exactly are Shades &quot;drawn&quot; to Duat? Like ghosts and the Underworld? A yearning? A feeling of pain if they linger too long in Neter Khertet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T08:47:12-07:00","id":1412726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1412659#post1412659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This article had some interesting thoughts on Bronze Age cultures and their ghosts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.worldhistory.org/img/c/p/1200x627/3218.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ghosts in the Ancient World </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ancient.eu/ghost/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A belief in an afterlife was central to every major civilization of the ancient world and this encouraged the recognition of the reality of ghosts as the spirits of the departed who, for one reason... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rereading Dreams of Avarice I noted this passage: &amp;quot;If you walk against the flow of<br /> Nebtet\u2019s blood it will dissolve you, and we five will fly to separate destinies. Your Shadow will howl in Neter-Khertet and the living will curse you. Your Spirit will invade your body and raise it to hunt the living who will burn you as an abomination. Your Essence will flow between Keb and Duat, to mingle in oases and holy places, and witches and unnatural things will devour it. Your Name will be forgotten and your Heart will sink alone to Duat, with no advocate, where She of the Countless Teeth will consume it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So if we assume the book accurately describes the fate that befalls non-Iremite educated souls, the Shadow seems like the best candidate for these Shades. The Ba survives, but seemingly animates the living corpse or otherwise lingers on in the physical remains. The Ka, perhaps playing of the similarity in names, seems to dissolve into magical energy that gets consumed by sorcerers, ghosts and spirits. No word about the fate of the Ren (odd) and the Ab falls into Duat and faces the Devourer. By this text a Shade could be the remnant of the Sheut, the Ren, or the Ab (since Shades are supposedly drawn slowly into Duat). Again, the shadowy nature seems to fit the Sheut best. That does beg the question if there are other ghostly entities out there born from the other pieces of the mortal. Also, I wonder about the general &amp;quot;population&amp;quot; of Shades- they presumably are fairly rare since Mummies alone know of them (likely because Shades are drawn to Sekhem). <br /> <br /> I also wonder if Shades ever serve cults the way the Blessed ghosts do/did in 1st edition. Do any serve the Devourer? How exactly are Shades &amp;quot;drawn&amp;quot; to Duat? Like ghosts and the Underworld? A yearning? A feeling of pain if they linger too long in Neter Khertet?</div> </div> </div> </div>On other ghostly soul parts: I would like to think so. I have some ideas for Ba spirits that I might tackle at some point, probably for the Vault.<br /> On shade populations: Shades are as common or as rare as you would like for your games. Shades are easily mistaken for ghosts when others encounter them, especially since most ghost powers work just fine on them. Shades also experience Neter-Khertet as a realm the way mummies do, and can use that to hide as well.<br /> Shade cultists: Maybe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you want shade cultists for your game?<br /> On being drawn to Duat: The pull of Duat isn\u2019t as strong as the Underworld\u2019s pull on ghosts. It\u2019s kind of like Duat is \u201cdownhill\u201d from them. Gravity pulls them in that direction, but they don\u2019t have to go right away. I would say that the hill becomes steeper the closer they get to the river or to a gateway into Duat, making it harder to fight gravity\u2019s pull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T08:41:16-07:00","id":1412852,"title":"","content":"I suppose first and foremost I just want to learn more about Shades and how they operate in Twilight and the Underworld. They seem a bit more sinister than Ghosts, given the preference for darkness and need for blood to be spilled, but their mindset is a little vague beyond &quot;like ghosts but not&quot;. The implication is that they don't obsess over objects and places or people from their living days, but they do seem to crave or need suffering to impose themselves on the living world. And they need some form of Sekhem to &quot;advance&quot; in power. Beyond this its all a bit vague what role they play in the lives of Mummies. And other denizens of the afterlife, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T13:29:49-07:00","id":1412886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1412852#post1412852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose first and foremost I just want to learn more about Shades and how they operate in Twilight and the Underworld. They seem a bit more sinister than Ghosts, given the preference for darkness and need for blood to be spilled, but their mindset is a little vague beyond &amp;quot;like ghosts but not&amp;quot;. The implication is that they don't obsess over objects and places or people from their living days, but they do seem to crave or need suffering to impose themselves on the living world. And they need some form of Sekhem to &amp;quot;advance&amp;quot; in power. Beyond this its all a bit vague what role they play in the lives of Mummies. And other denizens of the afterlife, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re deliberately left vague for now, so that each group can use them in the way that fits best for their game. That said, I\u2019d love the opportunity to expand upon them in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T07:01:25-07:00","id":1413221,"title":"","content":"I find myself how Hollow Mekhet are affected by all this and whether it would be possible to make one whole again? I definitely want to get Mummy next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T19:54:15-08:00","id":1433572,"title":"","content":"Old, but: Perhaps the Shade of a person <i>carries</i> the soul to Duat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T04:38:03-08:00","id":1433697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1433572#post1433572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old, but: Perhaps the Shade of a person <i>carries</i> the soul to Duat?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very reasonable explanation for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T10:49:34-08:00","id":1433724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1433697#post1433697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A very reasonable explanation for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The probably overly pedantic question that comes to my mind here is- what do we mean by &quot;soul&quot; in this context? Ghosts (i know, I know, ghosts aren't &quot;people&quot; they are &quot;psychic doubles&quot; of dead people or something like that)? The version of a &quot;soul&quot; that leads to various conditions if you lose it per the core rules? The soul of a mage, the part that allows them to do magic? Or one or more of the five parts of a soul that mummies believe? I'm sorry! Chronicles of Darkness are a little convoluted when it comes to this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T05:36:48-08:00","id":1433789,"title":"","content":"Well, from what we have between Mummy, Mage, some Demon and a little bit of the other gamelines, a &quot;soul&quot; seems to be the sense of higher self- a person is not their soul, but a soul is required to be a functional &quot;person&quot;. From Mage's perspective, it is a combination of their Mind, Fate, Prime, Spirit and Death, which are all tied together to create the person's connection to the Supernal. From Mummy's point of view, it is their Spirit, Name, Essence, Heart and Shadow, the five pillars which define someone's traits and eternal existence. The common idea that the soul is something which persists, a quality which relates to higher realities, and eventually leaves the world. Soul eaters destroy the collective entity which is a &quot;soul&quot; by breaking it to parts, and &quot;pieces&quot; of the soul seem to be imperfect representations of the person (probably like ghosts). In short, a soul is basically a quality which does not simply makes you who you are, but allows you to change, evolve, learn and grow, and without it you become stagnated and starts to &quot;spiritually rot&quot;. The soul is not &quot;you&quot; as much as you heart is not &quot;you&quot; and even your brain is not &quot;you&quot;- it is a spiritual &quot;body&quot; or &quot;organ&quot;, which connects the five parts which make you &quot;you&quot;, and allow the person to grow, change, learn- and eventually, be judged. Because someone without a soul can't be account responsible to their actions, and as such can't be punished for breaking rules which don't apply to them. For Mages, souls are what makes humanity divine. For the Judges, souls are what makes humanity a sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T20:30:51-08:00","id":1433978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1433724#post1433724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The probably overly pedantic question that comes to my mind here is- what do we mean by &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot; in this context? Ghosts (i know, I know, ghosts aren't &amp;quot;people&amp;quot; they are &amp;quot;psychic doubles&amp;quot; of dead people or something like that)? The version of a &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot; that leads to various conditions if you lose it per the core rules? The soul of a mage, the part that allows them to do magic? Or one or more of the five parts of a soul that mummies believe? I'm sorry! Chronicles of Darkness are a little convoluted when it comes to this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts aren\u2019t souls, but they most certainly are people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T13:03:35-08:00","id":1434174,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I still think Shades are the Sheut/Death arcana aligned aspect of the Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T13:14:52-08:00","id":1434175,"title":"","content":"While that's seems to be the intention, that leads to the question of if that's true, than: a) what are ghosts? b) what about the other parts of the soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T14:41:33-08:00","id":1434186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434175#post1434175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's seems to be the intention, that leads to the question of if that's true, than: a) what are ghosts? b) what about the other parts of the soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's go to the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreams of Avarice, Litany of the Fivefold Soul</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are the five who dwell within you and surround you. We are the hand that writes and the voice that speaks. We are the speech within that shapes your mouth and the spirit that moves your hand. Thus have we been bound into you, oh Deathless One, within a single, heavy drop of Sekhem, which flows between Keb and Duat upon the River and sinks along the Nebtet's red paths.<br /> <br /> Deathless One, know that when the rites have been completed [and] your flesh has been sanctified you will feel your body call, and an urge to re-enter it and walk the sunlit world again. Do not return! If you walk against the flow of Nebtet's blood it will dissolve you, and we five will fly to separate destinies. <b>Your Shadow will howl in Neter-Khertet and the living will curse you. Your Spirit will invade your body and raise it to hunt the living, who will burn you as an abomination. Your Essence will flow between Keb and Duat, to mingle in oases and holy places, and witches and unnatural things will devour it. Your Name will be forgotten, and your Heart will sink alone to Duat, with no advocate, where She of the Countless Teeth will consume it.</b> This is the first straying from the way of Deathlessness.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T15:06:57-08:00","id":1434188,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, the Dreams of Avarice- how could I have not checked the actual &quot;guide to the soul&quot;?<br /> <br /> So if the force which binds the soul together breaks, your Shadow/Death becomes a ghost, your Spirit/Mind becomes an hungry dead (probably a Vampire reference, but could also be a zombie or any other undead), your Essence/Prime is mixed in the world's ley lines, your Name/Fate gets forgotten and your Heart/Spirit is eaten by the Devourer. So if the Shades are a piece of the soul, it seems that by the book's analysis they fit more to the Heart, IMO, than the Shadow- but I personally view Shades as &quot;complete souls&quot;, with the Shadow being projected to serve as their body (we could also say that they are the &quot;howling Shadow in Neter Khertet&quot;, but that feels much more like ghost than like shade, and that again brings the question of <i>what are ghosts</i>).<br /> <br /> That also makes me think if each of the parts of the soul are &quot;sentient&quot;, perhaps like how the Shadow may be ghosts, the Spirit could be either the Beast or even the Strix, and maybe your Name could correspond to the Echoes from Demon- which are the burn remains of Covers which still haunt you (which is very fitting for &quot;forgotten names&quot;). I could imagine that Essence piece with a strong sense of identity could perhaps become a &quot;guardian spirit&quot; of a Loci or other place of power (like how Sentient Places are presented in Hunter 2e), while the Heart may be a clinging horror of some sort.... which also sounds like a ghost, except that ghosts are controlled by Death and not Spirit- so who knows? Could be its own ephemeral entity.<br /> <br /> (Also, what I find as extremely funny is that in a way, the Dreams of Avarice is the most supportive text to the ideology of the Keepers of the Source- for while Mage and Werewolf make their claims sound like nonsense, Dreams of Avarice basically says that <i>those creatures consume souls</i>, so using a Source could be seen as a &quot;bad thing&quot; (sure, you could argue it is not a &quot;complete soul&quot;, but still- not cool). Just wanted to point it out because it amused me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T15:45:43-08:00","id":1434193,"title":"","content":"I really do need to reread Dreams of Avarice. Sorry everyone.<br /> I had previously considered it as unreliable, in the same vein as the Book of the Deceived. And they were written in 1st edition, before Shades (and Fiends for that matter) were writen.<br /> But we shouldn't dismiss it; they are our sources.<br /> <br /> I will say that it has been confirmed multiple times that Ghosts aren't Souls, which implies to me they aren't 'part' of a soul either. Obviously that is an unpopular position and to be fair, nothing comes close to saying that in primary sources.<br /> That said, given how they do seem to focus more on memory for both Essence and as a currency between themselves (see the Absent in Geist 2nd), as well as the ultimate fate of them in the Underworld...i'd say they have more than a little nod to the Ren (Name) in the cited passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T16:45:14-08:00","id":1434200,"title":"","content":"Oh, I can't say that this is an unpopular opinion as I have no way to prove that my opinion is more popular :P Like, it could very well be that yours is the popular one. However, there are a few things which lead me to think about Ghosts as Sheut versus Shades-<br /> <br /> a) We know that ghosts are soulless- however, in my view, being a &quot;part&quot; of a soul doesn't mean that you have a soul. I mean, your skin is not &quot;you&quot;, but you are not &quot;you&quot; without your skin- or heart, or brain, or any other organ. Souls are a collective of five parts, so if you are only a part of it, you don't have a soul.<br /> <br /> b) Ghosts are the incarnation of the memory of the dead. Basically, they are small moments of &quot;Death&quot; that something leaves behind- and the idea of ephemeral pieces of Death which carry an uncanny resemblance to the person that left them behind really feels, IMO, like the presence of a Shadow pillar, unsupported by the others<br /> <br /> c) Again, the Dreams of Avarice description of Sheut which seems to be much more like ghosts than like shades. Shades seems more &quot;complete&quot;, from my reading, so it feels like they are more like &quot;ghosts which have souls&quot;- or basically, a complete soul, instead of just pieces of it.<br /> <br /> d) In Egyptian religion, the &quot;Shadow&quot; wasn't just a literal shadow, but any kind of imprint of the person- like paintings and sculptures. Ghosts are the imprints of the person who left them- making them into a &quot;Shadow&quot; by that definition. Sure, Iremite religion does not have to obey its real life parallel, but still, it should be noted.<br /> <br /> e) I think that the main reason for that view of mine is that I'm Jewish, and something which I think that wasn't really brought up as far as I'm aware that in Orthodox/mystical Judaism, the Soul is also a five parts entity! Those components are Nephesh (Spirit), Rukh (Ghost/Wind), Neshama (Soul- it's complicated), Haya (Living Thing) and Yehida (Unity). I'm not going to go through the whole &quot;Kabbalistic Soul Anatomy&quot; (again, it's complicated but could be applied through some creative interpretation to Mummy's concepts), but that basic idea is this- not everything has all five parts of the Soul. Animals, for example, have only Nephesh and Rukh, yet no &quot;higher units&quot;. So as this is a part of my system of belief, it makes sense to me that something could only have some parts of a soul without having a soul. Does the mysticism of Judaism apply to Mummy's cosmology? Probably not, but again, it somewhat fits, IMO. <br /> <br /> Again, nothing canon to support either claims, but that's just my view on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T13:07:44-08:00","id":1434520,"title":"","content":"I just love how we have these philosophical debates regarding the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T18:40:59-08:00","id":1434660,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;Your Shadow will howl in Neter-Khertet and the living will curse you.&quot;<br /> <br /> This could easily fit either the description of a ghost or a shade. Or something else<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Spirit will invade your body and raise it to hunt the living, who will burn you as an abomination.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most likely referencing a revenant or similar walking corpse. One could assume that any body animated by magic is powered by the Ba. Interesting to note that this switches the Ba and Ka seen in previous books- usually the Ka is what gets blamed for the corpse rising in old Irem, at least from the few references made to it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Essence will flow between Keb and Duat, to mingle in oases and holy places, and witches and unnatural things will devour it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Huh. So is this implying that the Ka and the &quot;Essence&quot; powering ghosts, spirits, werewolves, and Angels are the same thing? Interesting.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Name will be forgotten&quot;<br /> <br /> In my opinion, completely ambiguous and a good candidate for another entity stalking Twilight and Duat.<br /> <br /> &quot;and your Heart will sink alone to Duat, with no advocate, where She of the Countless Teeth will consume it.&quot;<br /> <br /> So according to this every unsanctified soul killed in ancient irem (and beyond?) is devoured by Ammit. So...did she &quot;save&quot; the leftovers the way she did with the Shuankhsen? How big an army is waiting down there in her maw?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T12:23:06-08:00","id":1434772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434660#post1434660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&amp;quot;Your Shadow will howl in Neter-Khertet and the living will curse you.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> This could easily fit either the description of a ghost or a shade. Or something else<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Your Spirit will invade your body and raise it to hunt the living, who will burn you as an abomination.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Most likely referencing a revenant or similar walking corpse. One could assume that any body animated by magic is powered by the Ba. Interesting to note that this switches the Ba and Ka seen in previous books- usually the Ka is what gets blamed for the corpse rising in old Irem, at least from the few references made to it.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Your Essence will flow between Keb and Duat, to mingle in oases and holy places, and witches and unnatural things will devour it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Huh. So is this implying that the Ka and the &amp;quot;Essence&amp;quot; powering ghosts, spirits, werewolves, and Angels are the same thing? Interesting.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Your Name will be forgotten&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In my opinion, completely ambiguous and a good candidate for another entity stalking Twilight and Duat.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;and your Heart will sink alone to Duat, with no advocate, where She of the Countless Teeth will consume it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So according to this every unsanctified soul killed in ancient irem (and beyond?) is devoured by Ammit. So...did she &amp;quot;save&amp;quot; the leftovers the way she did with the Shuankhsen? How big an army is waiting down there in her maw?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I knew more about the current canonical combination of Mage and Mummy regarding soul parts, but iir\u00e7, I had a few misgivings with it. For example, in Egyptian myth, the Ab is the seat of feelings and sentience, which to me screams Mind. Which would make sense, if it disappears into Duat with no protection. Yet at the same time, the Ba was that little voice in your head that is you, making choices and being self aware, which ALSO fits mind. Especially since a lot of Ba imagery involved the Ba being your self awareness flying out of your body much like astral travel. <br /> <br /> I do agree with the idea that just because a Ghost isn't a soul DOESNT mean that it isn't a FRAGMENT of the soul, or at least one of many echoes or shadows the soul created. Because Doppelgangers are a thing, I am hesitant to say a Ghost is the FULL Sheut, but certainly is one of the many shadows and echoes a soul created in the world. A soul with unfinished business or that has many near death experiences could create multiple ghosts, after all. None of which fit the bill to be the WHOLE sheut of a person. The Absent definitely add an interesting twist as they consume, harbor, and give away such echoes so often that they aren't even really the ghost of a single person anymore, but a magath-like amalgamation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T12:58:14-08:00","id":1434778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434772#post1434772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish I knew more about the current canonical combination of Mage and Mummy regarding soul parts, but iir\u00e7, I had a few misgivings with it. For example, in Egyptian myth, the Ab is the seat of feelings and sentience, which to me screams Mind. Which would make sense, if it disappears into Duat with no protection. Yet at the same time, the Ba was that little voice in your head that is you, making choices and being self aware, which ALSO fits mind. Especially since a lot of Ba imagery involved the Ba being your self awareness flying out of your body much like astral travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay that I can help with, though just a quick reminder that Mummy: The Curse is faux proto-ancient Egypt, so there is going to be some deviation.<br /> The cross over between M:Aw and M:tC in the Dark Eras Companion (Princes of the Conquered Land) is the primary source for this, though Dark Eras 1 does hint around these ideas in the To the Strongest chapter (thank the Weret-Hekau for that).<br /> As you may know, Mage associates the Soul with the 5 subtle Arcana, which in turn matches the whole &quot;5 Pillars of the Soul&quot; concept used in Mummy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DEC, page 137</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Ab: Spirit</li> <li>Ba: Mind</li> <li>Ka: Prime</li> <li>Ren: Fate</li> <li>Sheut: Death</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T13:33:35-08:00","id":1434781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434778#post1434778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay that I can help with, though just a quick reminder that Mummy: The Curse is faux proto-ancient Egypt, so there is going to be some deviation.<br /> The cross over between M:Aw and M:tC in the Dark Eras Companion (Princes of the Conquered Land) is the primary source for this, though Dark Eras 1 does hint around these ideas in the To the Strongest chapter (thank the Weret-Hekau for that).<br /> As you may know, Mage associates the Soul with the 5 subtle Arcana, which in turn matches the whole &amp;quot;5 Pillars of the Soul&amp;quot; concept used in Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I knew that they came to a canonical answer, and was part of the debates and theories before it was set in stone. And I can see it. Ab definitely fits with resonance and the emotions that reside in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Shades don't have anchors, but DO have memories. They clearly aren't Geists, but aren't Ghosts, either. It almost makes me wonder if there is a single pillar explanation at all,or if instead they are the partial remains of a ripped up soul with Remnants like a Shuanksen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T14:27:31-08:00","id":1434785,"title":"","content":"I want to add a little to the discussion about ghosts:<br /> While there's no reason to think they aren't related to the Sheut pillar (especially considering the text from Dreams of Avarice above), a lot of stuff regarding the formation of ghosts concerns strong emotions and Integrity breaking points. (The strength of human ghosts and thr likelyhood that they are formed at all are tied to their Integrity, while the strength of non-human ghosts are tied to how traumatic or important their death or destruction was to humans.) To me, that aspect seems more like it's tied to the Ba pillar. The Spirit is also what's said to create undead beings, which could refer to revenants (the kind that are ghosts possessing their own corpses; not the revenants from 2e VtR).<br /> On top of that ghosts gain Essence from being remembered. I think that implies a relationship with the Ren pillar as well.<br /> <br /> I absolutely believe that ghosts aren't &quot;a pillar&quot;, or even made from the parts of a pillar (since the formation of ghosts seems to have zero effect on the soul, given the existence of Doppelg\u00e4nger and how Mage makes no distinction between souls taken from the living and souls trapped after death), but I do think that there's still a connection. Rather than ghosts being detached parts of the soul, I would consider the soul to be the creator of ghosts, possibly the Spirit being what powers the process and the Shadow being the &quot;template&quot; around which a ghost is formed, or something like that. How the relationship would look is something I'd rather leave to someone more confident in their MtC lore to describe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, has anyone done a comparison between the various topics of this thread (ghosts, shades, the five pillars of the soul) with the Hollow Mekhet?<br /> For those who don't know, Mekhet is a Clan of vampires, and the Hollow Mekhet is the original variation of them, later replaced by regular Mekhet upon contact with other vampires. The Hollow Mekhet dates back to ancient Egypt (though in their Clanbook I think they're implied to be older still, quite possibly contemporary with the Nameless Empire) and are for all purposes vampires haunted by a &quot;ghost&quot; of their own. It is named the &quot;Ka&quot; and is said to be envious of the corporeal vampire. Ruleswise they're ghosts but instead of being in Twilight and being able to use Manifestations, they only appears in mirrors, phones, TVs, and such. Basically anything that can &quot;reflect&quot; a person somehow.<br /> I almost forgot: The other part that sets Hollow Mekhet aside from regular Mekhet (as well as all other vampires) is that they don't have an echo, a shadow or a reflection in the mirror, and never appears on any recordings. Basically, anything the vampire should be reflected in (except the echo and the shadow) it is the Ka that can take its place if it so chooses.<br /> Any thoughts about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T15:35:59-08:00","id":1434791,"title":"","content":"All that talk about how ghosts are connected to Integrity, trauma and memories made me think about something- dust at home is said to be around 50% dead human skin.<br /> <br /> And not only that- we cut our nails. Our hair drops naturally. Our spit is being carried away with every breath. Our oils leave fingerprints on whatever we touch. When we are wounded, we bleed. All of those pieces- skin, hair, nails, blood - all of those dead pieces, they aren't us. They are what remains of us. Our body constantly dies and being reborn, yet we are still we- all that dead matter, that's not us. Those are just pieces of us- and yet, if we were to examine those leftovers, we'll see that they still carry a trace to us. Our DNA, our protean- our own body keeps falling apart and fixing itself, leaving incomplete replicas of &quot;us&quot; everywhere. Ghosts could very well be basically that- they are not souls, but they are <i>of the soul</i>. Breaking points target our mind, by healthy Integrity and a healthy soul generally go together (for example, losing a Soul generally means that your Integrity is going to spiral down). Every time that someone goes through a breaking point, their soul is wounded- and we do know that soul can and do break, according to Deviant. Still, not every small scratch breaks the soul, and it is not impossible that the soul has some sort of an &quot;healing mechanism&quot; to fix itself after getting wounded- but some &quot;soul stuff&quot; still oozes out. Incomplete. Unbalanced. Broken. Pieces of ourselves which are not us. Dead remains which are of us.<br /> <br /> Ghosts may not be souls, but they very well be made from the same raw materials- only dead, and slowly rotting away. And just like how once people didn't believed that we could make organic material without life, it could be that it is only a matter of time before people could start making &quot;ghosts&quot; through artificial methods- in the Cyberpunk Shard, for example, AIs were presented as ghosts, after all. So yeah- ghosts may very well be us and be made from Pillars, yet still not be souls. And just like we fail at making life out of scratch, it is currently impossible to make souls out of the raw material... for now, at least.<br /> <br /> As for the Hollow Mekhet- IIRC, the Mekhet in their Clan Book were very tied to &quot;ghosts&quot;, especially their Hollow version, and it is a common theory that the first Hollow may have been the result of an experiment to recreate the Rite of Return (even if their Clan Book suggests that they may be older than humanity), but it could very well be that their creation is based around a manipulation of the dead person's Pillars in a way that relates to ghosts. IIRC, Hollows are created from desecrated burial, which could break the soul into its components- leaving their Reflection and Shadow fleeing the body to torment the living, while the other Pillars drive themselves into the dead body to feed upon the living. Yeah, the Hollow situation fits really well to the end result of &quot;what happens when the soul's Pillars get broken and scattered&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T17:14:16-08:00","id":1434797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434791#post1434791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts could very well be basically that- they are not souls, but they are <i>of the soul</i>. Breaking points target our mind, by healthy Integrity and a healthy soul generally go together (for example, losing a Soul generally means that your Integrity is going to spiral down). Every time that someone goes through a breaking point, their soul is wounded- and we do know that soul can and do break, according to Deviant. Still, not every small scratch breaks the soul, and it is not impossible that the soul has some sort of an &quot;healing mechanism&quot; to fix itself after getting wounded- but some &quot;soul stuff&quot; still oozes out. Incomplete. Unbalanced. Broken. Pieces of ourselves which are not us. Dead remains which are of us.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pi6aRRx-YQc\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Understand, that there is no point in living! Cry, that there is no answer! Where there is darkness, there are shadows! I, myself, am all of you humans!</i></a><br /> <br /> The modern Underworld is made of ghosts. This is, in fact, kind of the problem \u2014 to available evidence, the Ocean of Fragments at its nadir, which dissolves identity after countless Corpus-dissolving Rivers drawn from tributaries carrying the ghosts of all things downstream, is not <i>receding</i> so much as the &quot;land&quot; has <i>pushed</i> the top and bottom further apart. Where once there was a vast drowning pool that could convey ghosts through these steps in relatively direct order, now the persistent nature of the discontented dead has formed a maze of caverns and slums and sham-utopias from which the Chthonic Gods may draw worshippers to feed the awful mechanism that continues to build in the dark.<br /> <br /> It is a throughline between Mage, Mummy, and Beast that the beings that loom largest in the human soul in general are things of hunger, pain, and fear, and if ghosts are any indication, those things don't need the soul to stick around. The way geists work, in fact, seems to lean into that \u2014 those things meld with the trauma of death to form a powerful mantle around a ghost that's put the River in its guts, and the price of that power is that intimidation is just about the only thing they understand. Primal forces form the Key to the living world, which all sorts exploit.<br /> <br /> Nothing lasts forever, of course \u2014 that's a byword of this game even without multiple other sources for &quot;souls can be broken or destroyed&quot; \u2014 but there's evidently something close enough to imperishable about the human soul that traumatizing it creates byproducts lasting enough for an entire realm of existence to now be in serious need of cleanup due to the demonic scavenger-parasite infestation that's built a home in the mess.<br /> <br /> <i>The Judges said, &quot;Let there be pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Judges said, &quot;Let there be misery.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T11:58:49-08:00","id":1434966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434797#post1434797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Judges said, &quot;Let there be pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Judges said, &quot;Let there be misery.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The Cthonic Gods: <i>&quot;As Above, So Below.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T14:26:02-08:00","id":1435001,"title":"","content":"The God Machine: &quot;<i>What rises must fall. What has fallen may rise again</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T15:08:44-08:00","id":1435111,"title":"","content":"Well, the good news is that some of the entities of Duat are less harsh and malicious. Some of them aren't about eternal suffering. Much the opposite. They offer a path to freedom and liberation.<br /> <br /> Ammit is waiting for you. Whenever you've had enough, go to her. Be released.<br /> <br /> (Yeah, yeah, Sutekh too. But that takes a lot of work and energy and A'aru probably isn't even worth it anymore by this point.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T04:44:20-08:00","id":1436178,"title":"","content":"So with 2e being out and the shade rules being official, here is something that I felt that we should take into notice- we all know that ghosts are soulless because that like soulless mortals, their &quot;mentality&quot; is reversed- they gain the most from their Vice and the least from their Virtue, as following their lower nature feels just far more satisfying than following their ideals.<br /> <br /> And here is the thing- shades also have Virtue and Vice, and they are also reversed. <br /> <br /> That means that shades can't have a soul- if they had, then their Virtue and Vice should have acted normally (as again, the reversed situation was the main argument for ghosts being soulless). So in that case, they can't really &quot;carry the soul&quot; (well, unless they carry it like its their baby- they don't have it, but they physically hold it), and if they are just one Pillar, that supports the notion that being a part of a soul does not mean you have a soul (which supports the ghosts are also made of &quot;soulstuff&quot;, even if we can argue how exactly it happens). <br /> <br /> Just something to ponder about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T07:41:10-08:00","id":1436800,"title":"","content":"Except the \u201csoul\u201d as defined by other gamelines whose absence does that is probably just the Ka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T07:44:39-08:00","id":1436801,"title":"","content":"Not according to Mage? Both Mage and Mummy (the two gamelines who bother talking about what a Soul is) examine it as a five parts entity, and I don't think that Mummy 2e claims otherwise. Dark Eras even bothers to link the two gamelines together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T08:21:44-08:00","id":1436809,"title":"","content":"Mage is arguably a bit internally inconsistent on the matter, I assume on purpose to emphasize the explicit fact that no Awakened has really figured out what the deal with souls is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T08:41:17-08:00","id":1436813,"title":"","content":"Mages defines souls as being governed by five Arcana. This doesn't really mean five parts, but it does mean that souls according to Mage has a fivefold nature of sorts. Furthermore, each of these Arcana can be used to manipulate points of a corresponding Pillar (as described in one of the Dark Eras books) which confirms that when Mage talks about souls it most definitely means the entire thing, five Pillars and all. And since soul loss in Mage is the same soul loss in all other games (that feature soul loss), each of them also refers to the entire soul.<br /> Basically, if the soul as known in other games was just the Ka, then mages would only be able to use the corresponding Arcanum to interact with the soul rather than all five. (Muddying things a bit is that mages still primarily only uses the Death Arcanum to manipulate souls, and Death corresponds to the Sheut Pillar. (Meaning Ka is definitely not the correct Pillar.) They can still see souls with all five related Arcana and would in theory need all five Arcana to create souls if that is possible with mages' magics.)<br /> <br /> I think the soul can be likened to a garlic. When Mage and most other games refers to the soul they consider the entire bulb. But when Mummy refers to the soul, it goes in depth and refers to the (in this case) five different cloves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T08:31:15-08:00","id":1436997,"title":"","content":"Things gets muddied when you account for how<br /> <br /> 1. The oneiros is described as \u201cthe landscape of the soul\u201d but is retained after soul loss.<br /> <br /> 2. Ba is the seat of identity and personality, neither of which are significantly affected by soul loss or transplantation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T09:27:49-08:00","id":1437003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1436997#post1436997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things gets muddied when you account for how<br /> <br /> 1. The oneiros is described as \u201cthe landscape of the soul\u201d but is retained after soul loss.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1300490\">It isn't retained.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Ba is the seat of identity and personality, neither of which are significantly affected by soul loss or transplantation. </div> </div> </div>It kinda is, but not the way you might think. Soul loss is a gradual process that very much leads to the destruction of personality and quite possibly identity.<br /> You're right about soul transplants, though. Gaining a new soul doesn't overwrite your personality or anything. From a Mage perspective that's because the soul reshapes to fit the person. I don't know how that works or can work from a Mummy perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:20:23-08:00","id":1439690,"title":"","content":"i wonder what a rank 6 shade would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:43:00-08:00","id":1439694,"title":"","content":"I assume that such shades would be the equivalent of Greek Hero Cults or something, as instead of diluting themselves through the archetypes of death and becoming chthonic horrors like how ghosts do, shades could have a much stronger emphasis on their identity, and become venerated as respected paragons of their time. So yeah, a person ascending into &quot;godhood&quot; after death is more likely to be a shade than a ghost, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T13:45:33-07:00","id":1539943,"title":"","content":"Has anyone checked out the WoD manuals on Mirrors to see if there is anything there shedding light on vampire reflection, especially the Hollow Mekhet's?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about what framework to use for Shades in my games and I'm probably going to connect somehow to vampires and the Mekhet origin story cosmologically speaking, even if no vampires show up in the chronicles.<br /> <br /> As for ghosts, I see them tied to memories rather than to a soul pillar of the 5 (mummies have all 5 pillars but are deprived of memory).<br /> <br /> Memory is tied to Sekhem (of which the Shades are hungry) in that both can be harvested from vessels. So I see it possible that a ghost (or more than one) and a shade can both be born of a dead person, but perhaps only one of each individual (if memory serves me well and vessels are either used for Memory or for Sekhem, but not for both - if I'm right, I would draw an analogy with the ghost or shade produced at someone's death).<br /> <br /> Either way, I see shades are linked to someone's life force, which perhaps they miss not just in itself but as a binding agent to a living body. This can open the way for links to the Striges and vampires.<br /> <br /> This is all still under development. God willing, I will have clearer ideas after I reread some of the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T15:22:00-07:00","id":1539950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539943#post1539943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone checked out the WoD manuals on Mirrors to see if there is anything there shedding light on vampire reflection, especially the Hollow Mekhet's?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mekhet clanbook has a primer on ancient Egyptian soul anatomy, including theory on how the Hollow works, but it's also one of the clanbooks most up-front about the fact that information is not presented free of bias, particularly when it comes to in-universe documents prepared by in-universe characters for other in-universe characters.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the Ka (as the Soul of Sustenance) separates from your corpse and wanders around, bringing your shadow along with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (if memory serves me well and vessels are either used for Memory or for Sekhem, but not for both - if I'm right, I would draw an analogy with the ghost or shade produced at someone's death). </div> </div> </div>Only relics provide pure Sekhem, while vestiges provide Pillars, but you get Reminisce Beats for completely cannibalizing either type of vessel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T17:09:22-07:00","id":1539959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539950#post1539950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mekhet clanbook has a primer on ancient Egyptian soul anatomy, including theory on how the Hollow works, but it's also one of the clanbooks most up-front about the fact that information is not presented free of bias, particularly when it comes to in-universe documents prepared by in-universe characters for other in-universe characters.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the Ka (as the Soul of Sustenance) separates from your corpse and wanders around, bringing your shadow along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to read that book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539950#post1539950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only relics provide pure Sekhem, while vestiges provide Pillars, but you get Reminisce Beats for completely cannibalizing either type of vessel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Then a human may generate both a ghost and a shade. Perhaps I will houserule that shades come from humans with some supernatural power, including just the merit-based ones like Clairvoyance or Ritual Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> In all cases, I don't think I will link ghosts and shades to specific pillars because I see them already linked to other traits of the Arisen: Memory (ghosts, even if they don't actually do anything with Arisen memory) and Sekhem (shades).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T05:21:16-07:00","id":1539984,"title":"","content":"Update: I have looked into the Mekhet Clan Book. Here's my take, if anyone's interested.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of my chronicles, the Hollow Mekhet understanding of their reflection as the Ka is just how they framed it for themselves in terms of the Egyptian beliefs of their time. These beliefs are not the same as Irem: centuries have passed and the meaning of certain concepts has changed. I don't see a solid, useable connection between the Ka pillar of MtC and the Ka of the Hollow Mekhet, so they're just different things for me. The loss of reflection may have some interesting connection to the Mirrors books of WoD, but I have not looked at those yet and probably won't unless I start planning a Mekhet heavy VtR chronicle. There are many weird ephemeral creatures with unique rules in CoD, and the Hollow Mekhet's reflection is just one of these. The Iremite framework used by Mummies and the arcana system used by Mages are not sufficient to embrace or discern all the different permutations of these phenomena, so each creature focuses on those things they can perceive and interact with in a significant way. <br /> <br /> I do postulate, however, a connection between Shades, Striges and vampires in general. My current idea is that Striges are Shades that have managed somehow at some point to leave the Twilight and enter the physical world and stay there. They have similarities to the Shades (interest in blood, shadowy appearance), but the move from one dimension to the other has also made them different. One important difference is that while Shades remember being a person, Striges have forgotten who they were and where they came from, or have confused ideas about this. Given the Underworld's connection to loss of memory and identity, that's not hard to imagine, even without coming up with a specific reason like having drunk from a particular river. I wonder if, since ghosts become geists by drinking from the rivers, shades might become striges instead. Need to dig deeper in the Geist material to see if it makes sense.<br /> Vampires are another evolution of Striges, once they manage to take a body in a deeper way than just possession, but this deprives them again of memory, hence why vampires don't actually remember having connections to the Striges. But yes, they have a type of Strix inside, whose identities and memories have been drowned by the deceased/vampire's own. If we say Striges are Shades who have drunk from the rivers, like Geists are ghosts who have, then vampires are something somewhat analogous (but with plenty differences) to a Sin-Eater. <br /> <br /> There's a story of the early Mekhet wandering through the Duat, getting lost and trading blood to its denizens in exchange of directions, and thus becoming vampires/Mekhet. I may use that as a way to explain how some Shades became Striges if I don't use the drink from the rivers idea, but I have to define the details of that. Once Striges entered the world through these lost travelers and the deals with them and the blood exchange, they became a feature of the physical living world, and produced the other clans in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T07:11:11-07:00","id":1539989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539984#post1539984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purposes of my chronicles, the Hollow Mekhet understanding of their reflection as the Ka is just how they framed it for themselves in terms of the Egyptian beliefs of their time. These beliefs are not the same as Irem: centuries have passed and the meaning of certain concepts has changed. I don't see a solid, useable connection between the Ka pillar of MtC and the Ka of the Hollow Mekhet, so they're just different things for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Era &quot;Hunger in the Black Land&quot; notes that ghosts are typically seen as the Ka of the deceased, denied of nourishment, and this is roughly flush with the Book of Lasting Death's statement that the Arisen view spirits as functionally the Ka of the phenomena they represent working to prevent Creation from being unmade, which itself jives with Dreams of Avarice's Litany of the Fivefold Soul describing what happens to your Essence after death (if you do not successfully undergo the Rite of Return) in terms that sound an awful lot like pooling in loci (and possibly Hallows).<br /> <br /> The Weret-Hekau, the Egyptian Great Cult of mages that was still around by the time the Diamond was being formed, identified the Obrimos as the Path most strongly connected to the Ka, and the crossover mechanics in the Dark Era &quot;Princes of the Conquered Land&quot; indicate that this is largely accurate, given that mages can sense Pillar points in creatures or objects using the Ruling Arcana of the Path tied to that Pillar and the Arisen can use Awakened magical items that relate to their guild's purview by spending the corresponding Pillar.<br /> <br /> One of the characters in the Halifax setting, according to rumor, &quot;obsesses over vampires whose Ka have abandoned their bodies.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can definitely do whatever you like in your chronicle, but all of the above does not paint a picture of the phenomena being unrelated just because Irem and historic Ancient Egypt are separated by time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The loss of reflection may have some interesting connection to the Mirrors books of WoD, but I have not looked at those yet and probably won't unless I start planning a Mekhet heavy VtR chronicle. </div> </div> </div>World of Darkness: Mirrors is a book of system and setting hacks that has nothing to do with the deeper cosmology and metaphysics of Chronicles (before or after the rebranding).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a story of the early Mekhet wandering through the Duat, getting lost and trading blood to its denizens in exchange of directions, and thus becoming vampires/Mekhet. </div> </div> </div>I would be curious as to where this story is printed, seeing as before this thread I had not heard of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I may use that as a way to explain how some Shades became Striges if I don't use the drink from the rivers idea, but I have to define the details of that. Once Striges entered the world through these lost travelers and the deals with them and the blood exchange, they became a feature of the physical living world, and produced the other clans in different ways. </div> </div> </div>It's implicit verging on explicit that &quot;Strix,&quot; like &quot;Kindred,&quot; is an umbrella term referring to a number of different similar-enough-to-share-game-mechanics entities. There's a type of God-Machine-related demon in Hunter's Mortal Remains supplement that is described in terms that visually and behaviorally evoke a subtype of Strix. Werewolf 2e Core has bird-spirits in Tokyo that sound a lot like the Strix in terms of probable shape, ability to possess corpses, and antipathy for vampires, but the color of the eyes is wrong (red instead of gold) and werewolves have the senses to identify if something is a spirit. A Strix using Synthesis to create a new vampire creates a Kindred with a clan determined randomly or by the connections of the host rather than anything to do with the Strix itself. Again, your chronicle, your take, but looked at holistically this would just be one more multiple-choice backstory among dozens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T11:06:47-07:00","id":1539999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539984#post1539984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Mirrors books of WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors is a book about alternative realities/hacking the game system for alternative settings.<br /> <br /> It is not a book about literal mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T11:12:54-07:00","id":1540000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Era &quot;Hunger in the Black Land&quot; notes that ghosts are typically seen as the Ka of the deceased, denied of nourishment, and this is roughly flush with the Book of Lasting Death's statement that the Arisen view spirits as functionally the Ka of the phenomena they represent working to prevent Creation from being unmade, which itself jives with Dreams of Avarice's Litany of the Fivefold Soul describing what happens to your Essence after death (if you do not successfully undergo the Rite of Return) in terms that sound an awful lot like pooling in loci (and possibly Hallows).</div> </div> </div> </div>You'e saying that Dark Era &quot;Hunger in the Black Land&quot; links the ghosts with the Ka. But Book of Lasting Death says that Arises see the spirits as the Ka of things. This is a contradiction in the system because, for Book of Lasting Death, spirits are those that interact with werewolves, and are different from ghosts as well as shades. Book of Lasting Death also says that everything generates a spirit except humans and the supernaturals that leave among them. But we also know from Mummy the Curse 2e that the soul of the Arisen has 5 pillars, one being the Ka, therefore what Ka means as a pillar and what it means as the spirit of something is related but not exactly the same. MtC2e, in its descriptions of the pillar of Ka or Essence does not speak much of &quot;eating&quot; or related ideas, but one may say that eating is the way the essence endures, and enduring and persevering are indeed meanings associated with the Ka pillar, as well as protecting. Book of Lasting Death says the spirits eat each other as a way of preserving creation - so this can work in terms of connections. But because humans and the supernatural among them do not produce a Ka, there is still a difference between the spirit of things and the Ka pillar of the soul - whether the soul in general, if all humans have a five fold soul but only Arisen keep that framework relevant, or the soul of the Arisen in particular. The soul also has Memory and Sekhem, but these concepts are handled differently in the case of mummies because of their specific condition.<br /> Dream of Avarice is 1st ed. It's surely a great resource for ideas (same reason why I looked into the Mekhet clan book, which is also 1st ed, or I'm curious about the Mirrors books), but I do try to use 2e material to &quot;tidy up&quot; some 1e ideas. So I think the passage you quoted is fantastic, and it actually makes sense with Essence=Ka=spirit to the limited extent of my familiarity with the metaphysics of Mage, Werewolf and the other lines. But had it said something conflicting with statements in 2e books, I might have dropped it.<br /> In VtR2E, one of the three suggested origins for the Mekhets is that they lost their Ka - an obvious hint at the Hollow Mekhet of 1st ed. If I look at what these Hollow Mekhet do in the only source on them (the Mekhet clan book), their Ka is their reflection and spirit of nourishment, whose gone rogue and appears in reflections and echoes and feeds on dead things unless it's presented properly blessed food. The idea of it being the spirit of nourishment is fine: nourishment is how things are preserved and we have already established the relationship between Ka, Spirit, Essence, eating and preservation. However the idea of the reflection is new: it does not relate to anything I know about spirits or Ka in MtC or other lines. This is why I say that I don't want to validate the Ka of the Mekhet as the Ka of Arisen. Not fully at least. What Hollow Mekhet are haunted by is not just their spirit. First, Book of Lasting Death says they shouldn't produce a spirit at all; second, spirits are not people's reflections and echoes and don't haunt them through that if separated from them. So I take it that what the Hollow Mekhet have lost and haunts them is a specific type of ephemera - as there are many in CoD unique to specific lines - which is not really the Ka itself, but it may be a part of it, or be close enough to it that it was identified as such by the Egyptian Mekhet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Weret-Hekau, the Egyptian Great Cult of mages that was still around by the time the Diamond was being formed, identified the Obrimos as the Path most strongly connected to the Ka, and the crossover mechanics in the Dark Era &quot;Princes of the Conquered Land&quot; indicate that this is largely accurate, given that mages can sense Pillar points in creatures or objects using the Ruling Arcana of the Path tied to that Pillar and the Arisen can use Awakened magical items that relate to their guild's purview by spending the corresponding Pillar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with Arisen and Mages having compatible metaphysics and mechanics. Crossovers would be difficult otherwise. I lack the familiarity with MtA and Dark Eras to pursue the connections more in detail, but my point was that there's no problem if the Ka that haunts the Mekhets is not 100% the same that Arisen and Mage would have in mind. It could be a specific form of it that operates on a frequency between those mages and Arisen are familiar with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can definitely do whatever you like in your chronicle, but all of the above does not paint a picture of the phenomena being unrelated just because Irem and historic Ancient Egypt are separated by time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say they are unrelated (in the sense of what I have said up to now, that the Mekhet Ka/reflection behaves differently from spirits and from the Arisen's Ka) not because of the separation by time, but because I objectively have no solid narrative hook to connect the idea of reflection and echo and shadow as a single haunting ephemera to the known explanation of Ka as the spirit of things and as the nourishing part of the soul. They are connected in the words and experience of the Hollow Mekhet, and based on Egyptian thought <i>as they report or recall it</i>, but I can't see corroborating evidence for this in MtC. So I have to conclude that there is a degree of cultural difference, easily justified through the time distance and the fact the the Mekhet experience can be unique, and they frame it according to their own understanding of the beliefs they were raised with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Darkness: Mirrors is a book of system and setting hacks that has nothing to do with the deeper cosmology and metaphysics of Chronicles (before or after the rebranding).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two Mirrors books to my knowledge. I thought it was about how to use creepy and magical mirrors and &quot;world-behind-the-mirror&quot; as part of World of Darkness stories. That's one reason why I thought it may shed light on the Mekhet predicament and reflections as haunting ephemera. But if the books are not about creepy mirrors, then nothing, I guess. Notice that VtR2E core manual gives a story about a queen and a mirror as one of the 3 possible origin stories of the Mekhet, and the Mekhet clan book, when I was looking through the contents and the titles of the sections, gave me the impression of also containing a story along these lines, but I didn't go to actual page and read it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be curious as to where this story is printed, seeing as before this thread I had not heard of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's in Mekhet clan book (didn't see it while skimming through the book), but it is given in VtR2e core manual as one of the 3 possible origin stories for the Mekhet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539989#post1539989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's implicit verging on explicit that &quot;Strix,&quot; like &quot;Kindred,&quot; is an umbrella term referring to a number of different similar-enough-to-share-game-mechanics entities. There's a type of God-Machine-related demon in Hunter's Mortal Remains supplement that is described in terms that visually and behaviorally evoke a subtype of Strix. Werewolf 2e Core has bird-spirits in Tokyo that sound a lot like the Strix in terms of probable shape, ability to possess corpses, and antipathy for vampires, but the color of the eyes is wrong (red instead of gold) and werewolves have the senses to identify if something is a spirit. A Strix using Synthesis to create a new vampire creates a Kindred with a clan determined randomly or by the connections of the host rather than anything to do with the Strix itself. Again, your chronicle, your take, but looked at holistically this would just be one more multiple-choice backstory among dozens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with Stryx being an umbrella term like Kindred. It makes perfect sense. And I had forgotten that the clan of a vampire they create is random, but that also poses no issue for me. It even makes more sense and is easier to use to make Stryx the main originator of vampire clans (while nothing prevents some clans to have another origin), with their differences. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T11:15:26-07:00","id":1540001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1539999#post1539999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mirrors is a book about alternative realities/hacking the game system for alternative settings.<br /> <br /> It is not a book about literal mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the correction. I was misled by the title. After all, one <i>can</i> make horror and creepy stories about mirrors. Mirror mirror on the wall... Alice through the Looking-glass (but made creepier)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T14:13:46-07:00","id":1540011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1540000#post1540000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'e saying that Dark Era &quot;Hunger in the Black Land&quot; links the ghosts with the Ka. But Book of Lasting Death says that Arises see the spirits as the Ka of things. This is a contradiction in the system because, for Book of Lasting Death, spirits are those that interact with werewolves, and are different from ghosts as well as shades. Book of Lasting Death also says that everything generates a spirit except humans and the supernaturals that leave among them. But we also know from Mummy the Curse 2e that the soul of the Arisen has 5 pillars, one being the Ka, therefore what Ka means as a pillar and what it means as the spirit of something is related but not exactly the same. MtC2e, in its descriptions of the pillar of Ka or Essence does not speak much of &quot;eating&quot; or related ideas, but one may say that eating is the way the essence endures, and enduring and persevering are indeed meanings associated with the Ka pillar, as well as protecting. Book of Lasting Death says the spirits eat each other as a way of preserving creation - so this can work in terms of connections. But because humans and the supernatural among them do not produce a Ka, there is still a difference between the spirit of things and the Ka pillar of the soul - whether the soul in general, if all humans have a five fold soul but only Arisen keep that framework relevant, or the soul of the Arisen in particular. The soul also has Memory and Sekhem, but these concepts are handled differently in the case of mummies because of their specific condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a contradiction for the spirits of things that aren't human and the ghosts of humans to both be thought of as the Ka of their respective phenomena. They are ephemeral beings powered by Essence that they get from consuming things like themselves and remaining in proximity to such things, and once deprived of their Anchors ghosts are more readily given to consumptive behavior, including but not limited to cannibalism such as that endemic to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dream of Avarice is 1st ed. It's surely a great resource for ideas (same reason why I looked into the Mekhet clan book, which is also 1st ed, or I'm curious about the Mirrors books), but I do try to use 2e material to &quot;tidy up&quot; some 1e ideas. So I think the passage you quoted is fantastic, and it actually makes sense with Essence=Ka=spirit to the limited extent of my familiarity with the metaphysics of Mage, Werewolf and the other lines. But had it said something conflicting with statements in 2e books, I might have dropped it. </div> </div> </div>In case it wasn't clear, I was saying that the inference to be made from the passage in Dreams is that the Essence that sustains ephemeral beings and empowers and is leveraged by mages and werewolves is related to the Pillar of the same name, which tracks with that Pillar aligning with the Path whose phenomena concern sources of magical and physical power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In VtR2E, one of the three suggested origins for the Mekhets is that they lost their Ka - an obvious hint at the Hollow Mekhet of 1st ed. </div> </div> </div>That same origin story is a direct nod to the origin story of the Ascending Ones from Hunter, who were the Cult of the Phoenix that story says fell. The history surrounding Akhenaten is deliberately kind of a mess of conflicting reports.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I look at what these Hollow Mekhet do in the only source on them (the Mekhet clan book), their Ka is their reflection and spirit of nourishment, whose gone rogue and appears in reflections and echoes and feeds on dead things unless it's presented properly blessed food. The idea of it being the spirit of nourishment is fine: nourishment is how things are preserved and we have already established the relationship between Ka, Spirit, Essence, eating and preservation. However the idea of the reflection is new: it does not relate to anything I know about spirits or Ka in MtC or other lines. </div> </div> </div>The clanbook posits that the shadow goes with the Ka when it wanders, and whether you call it the Sheut or the Khaibit the metaphysical description of what the &quot;shadow&quot; of is as a part of someone's soul is described the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I say that I don't want to validate the Ka of the Mekhet as the Ka of Arisen. Not fully at least. What Hollow Mekhet are haunted by is not just their spirit. </div> </div> </div>Correct. It's their ghost, in all the mechanical and thematic senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, Book of Lasting Death says they shouldn't produce a spirit at all; second, spirits are not people's reflections and echoes and don't haunt them through that if separated from them. So I take it that what the Hollow Mekhet have lost and haunts them is a specific type of ephemera - as there are many in CoD unique to specific lines - which is not really the Ka itself, but it may be a part of it, or be close enough to it that it was identified as such by the Egyptian Mekhet. </div> </div> </div>See above: the Ka that haunts the Hollow Mekhet is a ghost. The book the Hollow were introduced in has its sample Hollow's Ka summoned for direct conversation by a character with a published statblock (Catesby from Shadows of the United Kingdom) that includes Death and Prime but no Spirit. 2e's mechanics for the Hollow in Thousand Years of Night explicitly models the Ka as a ghost, which jives with Hunger in the Black Land's statement on how ghosts are generally perceived in terms of soul-anatomy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I say they are unrelated (in the sense of what I have said up to now, that the Mekhet Ka/reflection behaves differently from spirits and from the Arisen's Ka) not because of the separation by time, but because I objectively have no solid narrative hook to connect the idea of reflection and echo and shadow as a single haunting ephemera to the known explanation of Ka as the spirit of things and as the nourishing part of the soul. They are connected in the words and experience of the Hollow Mekhet, and based on Egyptian thought <i>as they report or recall it</i>, but I can't see corroborating evidence for this in MtC. So I have to conclude that there is a degree of cultural difference, easily justified through the time distance and the fact the the Mekhet experience can be unique, and they frame it according to their own understanding of the beliefs they were raised with. </div> </div> </div>The Hollow Mekhet's Ka behaves in a way consistent with the more horror-story-toned ghosts that the setting is generally concerned with as the more visible divergences from the quieter &quot;Rank 2 person who happens to be dead&quot; and all the references to the Ka as it correlates to hunger concern it as an entity separated from the body.<br /> <br /> The Ka of the Arisen is a Ka in a nominally-living body made eternal; the Obrimos have the hardest time learning the Death Arcanum used for ghosts despite being identified with the Ka, so evidently the part of the soul that distinguishes a living body from a dead one doesn't work the same way in living bodies as it does in dead ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notice that VtR2E core manual gives a story about a queen and a mirror as one of the 3 possible origin stories of the Mekhet, and the Mekhet clan book, when I was looking through the contents and the titles of the sections, gave me the impression of also containing a story along these lines, but I didn't go to actual page and read it. </div> </div> </div>The story in VtR2e Core is part of a larger pattern of fairy tale-styled origin stories pretty directly riffing on the tale of Snow White \u2014 the equivalent stories for the Nosferatu, Gangrel, Ventrue, and Daeva evoke the seven dwarves, the huntsman, the prince, and the titular princess (notably, the Nosferatu, Daeva, and Ventrue stories cannot all have the same princess). The Mekhet story is evoking the witch with her magic mirror, in no small part because mirrors are an evocative narrative device in general.<br /> <br /> There is no similar origin story in the Mekhet clanbook, which simply uses mirrors in the described capacity for showing the Ka's manifestations and the signs of its absence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if it's in Mekhet clan book (didn't see it while skimming through the book), but it is given in VtR2e core manual as one of the 3 possible origin stories for the Mekhet. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that the word &quot;Duat&quot; doesn't appear anywhere in that story, I get the distinct feeling if they were referring to a specific underworld in the Chronicles cosmology it wouldn't be the one where the river and oases are made of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T12:43:34-07:00","id":1540060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1540011#post1540011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a contradiction for the spirits of things that aren't human and the ghosts of humans to both be thought of as the Ka of their respective phenomena. They are ephemeral beings powered by Essence that they get from consuming things like themselves and remaining in proximity to such things, and once deprived of their Anchors ghosts are more readily given to consumptive behavior, including but not limited to cannibalism such as that endemic to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> In case it wasn't clear, I was saying that the inference to be made from the passage in Dreams is that the Essence that sustains ephemeral beings and empowers and is leveraged by mages and werewolves is related to the Pillar of the same name, which tracks with that Pillar aligning with the Path whose phenomena concern sources of magical and physical power.<br /> <br /> That same origin story is a direct nod to the origin story of the Ascending Ones from Hunter, who were the Cult of the Phoenix that story says fell. The history surrounding Akhenaten is deliberately kind of a mess of conflicting reports.<br /> <br /> The clanbook posits that the shadow goes with the Ka when it wanders, and whether you call it the Sheut or the Khaibit the metaphysical description of what the &quot;shadow&quot; of is as a part of someone's soul is described the same.<br /> <br /> Correct. It's their ghost, in all the mechanical and thematic senses.<br /> <br /> See above: the Ka that haunts the Hollow Mekhet is a ghost. The book the Hollow were introduced in has its sample Hollow's Ka summoned for direct conversation by a character with a published statblock (Catesby from Shadows of the United Kingdom) that includes Death and Prime but no Spirit. 2e's mechanics for the Hollow in Thousand Years of Night explicitly models the Ka as a ghost, which jives with Hunger in the Black Land's statement on how ghosts are generally perceived in terms of soul-anatomy.<br /> <br /> The Hollow Mekhet's Ka behaves in a way consistent with the more horror-story-toned ghosts that the setting is generally concerned with as the more visible divergences from the quieter &quot;Rank 2 person who happens to be dead&quot; and all the references to the Ka as it correlates to hunger concern it as an entity separated from the body.<br /> <br /> The Ka of the Arisen is a Ka in a nominally-living body made eternal; the Obrimos have the hardest time learning the Death Arcanum used for ghosts despite being identified with the Ka, so evidently the part of the soul that distinguishes a living body from a dead one doesn't work the same way in living bodies as it does in dead ones.<br /> <br /> The story in VtR2e Core is part of a larger pattern of fairy tale-styled origin stories pretty directly riffing on the tale of Snow White \u2014 the equivalent stories for the Nosferatu, Gangrel, Ventrue, and Daeva evoke the seven dwarves, the huntsman, the prince, and the titular princess (notably, the Nosferatu, Daeva, and Ventrue stories cannot all have the same princess). The Mekhet story is evoking the witch with her magic mirror, in no small part because mirrors are an evocative narrative device in general.<br /> <br /> There is no similar origin story in the Mekhet clanbook, which simply uses mirrors in the described capacity for showing the Ka's manifestations and the signs of its absence.<br /> <br /> Setting aside that the word &quot;Duat&quot; doesn't appear anywhere in that story, I get the distinct feeling if they were referring to a specific underworld in the Chronicles cosmology it wouldn't be the one where the river and oases are made of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>We see this element of the setting differently, and have a different take on some passages. Given the nature of CoD and nWoD as a toolbox for STs, no big issue. And I believe some things have been deliberately left undefined, while others may even be intentionally contradictory so that their mystery can't be solved in a definite way. It leaves STs more room, it stimulates discussion and curiosity, and it leads different players to develop different categories to make sense of what's in the CoD - case in point, the meaning of Ka and the nature of the Hollow Mekhet's Reflection. The clanbook says the Reflection is a ghost with some unique characteristics (that have little to do with ghosts). I read that as: it's an ephemera, with the rules of ghosts (like other ephemera) plus its special exceptions (like other ephemera), so it's not an actual ghost, but something different. You read it as &quot;it's a ghost.&quot; I find both acceptable readings, though I prefer mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T07:35:27-07:00","id":1540202,"title":"","content":"Given the context of the thread, it is entirely possible that a death aligned Twilight entity which lives in mirrors and comes from a specific supernatural source (aka Hollowing out of Mekhets, however that happens...) Is not a ghost but a shade, or is neither but a third type of Ephemeral entity.<br /> <br /> All of which could be called variously shades, ghosts, geister, or whatever you wanted...<br /> <br /> <br /> You milage/table may vary.<br /> <br /> I note however the Mekhet origin story (in Requiem 2e) refers to a demon eating people's Hearts (Ab) and the Priests of Set removing their Essence (Ka).<br /> <br /> There is discussion of Shades (Sheut) carrying the Heart (Ab) of the dead down to Duat (for judgement) - which may explain Shades...<br /> <br /> We also know one of the explaination of the Strix was as the things which should have been spirits of humans but humans have (five-fold) souls instead? So it is like Strix became something different by being disconnected from their material part.<br /> <br /> It makes sense then if human souls contain something like a spirit... And then Strix merging with Human amounts to a form of Claiming. Though with them as the 'natural' entity which can fully merge still with humans to become (a type of) kindred.<br /> <br /> I am still not clear on why removing one's essence would protect one from something which tries to eat a heart, or how that turns them into vampires...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T08:12:17-07:00","id":1540207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1540202#post1540202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still not clear on why removing one's essence would protect one from something which tries to eat a heart, or how that turns them into vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter: the Vigil: Witch Finders contains an account from the Ascending Ones of an army of spirit-ridden mechanical insects, including an ant that consumed and replaced the physical heart of the apocryphal queen Nitocris. This is more of that &quot;the events of the time of Akhenaten are full of conflicting reports&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}